<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
  <span class="pill">OPEN SOURCE · MIT · LOCAL-FIRST</span>
  <h1>You say it.<br>Witness <em>proves</em> it.</h1>
  <p class="sub">Experience your product and talk naturally — “this button does nothing”. Witness welds every word to the causal evidence of that exact second: clicks, requests, errors, DOM state, full replay. Then hands the package to your AI coding agent.</p>
  <div class="install"><b>$</b> npm i -g github:wookat/witness<button title="copy" onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText('npm i -g github:wookat/witness')">⧉</button></div>
  <div class="cta">
    <a class="btn pri" href={GH}>View on GitHub</a>
    <a class="btn" href="#how">How it works ↓</a>
  </div>
</div></header>

<section><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">The problem</div>
  <h2>Agents can't see what you see.</h2>
  <p class="lede">A human notices “the button fades weirdly when I scroll” in two seconds. Writing that up for an AI agent takes ten minutes of screenshots, element selectors and prompt crafting — and the result still loses the <i>why</i>. Voice is the cheapest annotation channel there is; it just never had a recorder.</p>
</div></section>

<section id="how"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">How it works</div>
  <h2>Three recording lines, one timeline.</h2>
  <p class="lede"><code>wit start &lt;dev-url&gt;</code> opens a managed browser. From that moment, three streams run in parallel — zero manual work:</p>
  <div class="grid g3">
    <div class="card"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Your voice</h3><p>Continuous audio + live speech-to-text. Say everything on your mind — one take, many issues, no need to split.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Operations + causal bursts</h3><p>Every click captures its ~1.8s aftermath: requests, responses, console errors, DOM changes. A click with <i>no</i> aftermath is itself evidence.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Page evolution</h3><p>rrweb full-DOM replay + event-driven screenshots + periodic DOM snapshots. Rewind the exact page state at any second.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="flow" style="margin-top:30px">
    <span><b>wit start</b> &lt;url&gt;</span><i>→</i>
    <span>browse + talk</span><i>→</i>
    <span>Ctrl+click / M to mark</span><i>→</i>
    <span>■ stop</span><i>→</i>
    <span><b>evidence package</b></span>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="evidence"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">The output</div>
  <h2>Your words become evidence anchors.</h2>
  <p class="lede">Each spoken fragment becomes a block on a timeline with the causal facts of that moment attached — the “causal burst”. This is what your agent actually reads:</p>
  <div class="term">
    <div class="th"><i></i><i></i><i></i>&nbsp;session.md</div>
<pre><span class="c-say">### 00:09 · SAY</span>
&gt; [00:15] <span class="c-say">"the button fades and shrinks when I scroll"</span>
<span class="c-dim">- `00:08`  SCROLL y=3936</span>
- `00:08`  <span class="c-acc">MUT</span>  `button.feedback` data-collapsed: false → true
- `00:11`  <span class="c-acc">MUT</span>  `button.feedback` data-collapsed: true → false   <span class="c-dim">← flapping on the boundary</span>

<span class="c-say">### 00:34 · SAY</span>
&gt; [00:34] <span class="c-say">"the submit button does nothing"</span>
- `00:33`  <span class="c-ok">CLICK</span> `button#submit` “提交” · @482,701
  <span class="c-dim">└─ (page did nothing for 1.8s after the click — that itself is evidence)</span>

<span class="c-say">### 01:02 · SAY</span>
&gt; [01:02] <span class="c-say">"the orders API returns wrong data"</span>
- `01:01`  <span class="c-ok">CLICK</span> `a[href="/orders"]` “订单”
  - `01:01`  <span class="c-dim">NET →</span> GET /api/orders?page=1
  - `01:01`  <span class="c-bad">NET ←</span> **200** /api/orders · [body](bodies/req_0041.json)   <span class="c-dim">← items: []</span></pre>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">Two audiences, one package</div>
  <h2>Humans get a replay. Agents get a structure.</h2>
  <div class="split">
    <div class="card aud h"><h4>For humans</h4><ul>
      <li>review.html <span>— speech cards + audio seek + screenshots</span></li>
      <li>▶ DOM replay <span>— embedded rrweb player, real page states</span></li>
      <li>film strip <span>— scrub the session like a video</span></li>
      <li>audio.webm <span>— the original take</span></li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="card aud"><h4>For AI agents</h4><ul>
      <li>PROMPT.md <span>— handoff instructions + page vocabulary</span></li>
      <li>session.md <span>— the evidence timeline above</span></li>
      <li>events.jsonl <span>— complete raw stream, crash-safe</span></li>
      <li>dom/ · bodies/ · shots/ <span>— snapshots, payloads, frames</span></li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="mcp"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">Pull, don't push</div>
  <h2><code>wit mcp</code> — evidence as an API.</h2>
  <p class="lede">Instead of a static dump, the session becomes a stdio MCP server. Point any MCP-capable agent at it and it queries exactly the evidence it needs:</p>
  <div class="grid g3">
    <div class="card"><h3><code>list_says</code></h3><p>Every spoken fragment with timestamps — the issue anchors.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><code>events_around</code></h3><p>Raw events in a time window, filtered by kind.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><code>get_dom_state</code></h3><p>Full DOM HTML nearest to a timestamp.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><code>get_errors</code></h3><p>Console errors, page errors, HTTP ≥ 400.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><code>get_shot / get_body</code></h3><p>Screenshot frames and response payloads on demand.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3><code>session_md</code></h3><p>The rendered timeline when the agent wants it all.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">Principles</div>
  <h2>Evidence never lies.</h2>
  <div class="grid g2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Local-first, zero config</h3><p>System Edge/Chrome + Edge SpeechRecognition — free real-time transcription, no API key, works anywhere. Cloud ASR and LLM polish are optional layers, never the pipeline.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Words are never rewritten</h3><p>Your speech lands verbatim in events.jsonl. Merging, correction and association are display-layer suggestions — the raw testimony stays auditable.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Evidence ≠ intent</h3><p>Clicks and scrolls are facts, not complaints. Without a spoken anchor, agents are told explicitly: never infer a bug from behavior alone.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Privacy engineered in</h3><p>Password fields masked in four channels; POST bodies redact credential fields; P freezes everything, mic included; <code>WIT_NO_BODIES</code> for sensitive apps.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section id="install"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="kicker">Install & run</div>
  <h2>Two minutes to your first evidence package.</h2>
  <div class="term">
    <div class="th"><i></i><i></i><i></i>&nbsp;terminal</div>
<pre><span class="c-dim"># needs Node 18+ and system Edge/Chrome — no downloads, no keys</span>
npm i -g github:wookat/witness
wit start http://localhost:5173     <span class="c-dim"># managed browser opens — talk & click</span>
<span class="c-dim"># stop → .witness/sessions/&lt;ts&gt;/  — feed PROMPT.md + dir to your agent</span>

wit list                            <span class="c-dim"># your sessions</span>
wit mcp                             <span class="c-dim"># serve the latest as an MCP server</span></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="cta" style="justify-content:flex-start">
    <a class="btn pri" href={GH}>★ Star on GitHub</a>
    <a class="btn" href={GH + "/blob/main/VISION.md"}>Read the vision ↗</a>
  </div>
</div></section>

